# Java Engineering Cheat Sheet Posts

Reference implementation: `content/java-engineering/primitive-data-types.md`, `content/java-engineering/hashmap.md`

## Repo Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `content/java-engineering/_index.md` | Section landing page |
| `content/java-engineering/<topic>.md` | One page per topic |
| `data/java_engineering_modules.yaml` | Module grouping and topic order |
| `data/java_cheatsheet_order.yaml` | Flat topic order (prev/next nav) |
| `layouts/shortcodes/java-note.html` | Note callout |
| `layouts/shortcodes/java-tip.html` | Tip callout |
| `layouts/shortcodes/java-warning.html` | Warning callout |

URL pattern: `/java-engineering/<filename>/`

## Scope

**In scope:** Core Java, OOP, collections, exceptions, generics, functional programming, streams, concurrency, memory, JVM, modern Java versions, IO, reflection, serialization, interview quick refs.

**Out of scope (separate sections):** Spring Boot, Hibernate, JPA, Maven, Gradle, design patterns, DSA, system design.

## Hugo Front Matter

```yaml
---
title: "<Topic Title>"
date: 2026-06-30T10:00:00+00:00
draft: true
description: "One-line summary for SEO."
tags: ["java", "java-cheatsheet", "<topic-tag>"]
categories: ["Java Engineering Handbook"]
shortTitle: "<Short Title>"
module: 1
moduleTitle: "Core Java Fundamentals"
sectionRef: "1.1"
ShowToc: true
javaVersions: ["8", "11", "17", "21", "25"]
---
```

Set `draft: false` when the page is ready to publish.

## Required Sections (use `##` headings)

Every topic page uses the same structure (collapsible via `sd-collapsible-content`):

1. **Executive Summary** — simple English overview
2. **Why It Exists** — problem/solution table
3. **Key Concepts** — Mermaid diagram + tables
4. **Syntax** — concise code + reference table
5. **Example** — small runnable Java snippet
6. **Internal Working** — JVM/runtime behavior; optional sequence diagram
7. **Common Mistakes** — bullets + `java-warning` where needed
8. **Best Practices** — production recommendations
9. **Interview Questions** — `interview-answer` shortcode blocks
10. **Related Topics** — internal links (prev/next + index)

Separate major sections with `---` horizontal rules.

## Callouts

```markdown
{{% note %}}
